<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills 26 pct sold, yield 17.32 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills 26 pct sold, yield 17.32 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's finance ministry offer of 20 billion levs of four-week discount T-bills was 26 percent sold, yielding 17.32 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		     BG3010297003</p>
<p> Par value			  20 billion levs</p>
<p> Auction date		     January 6, 1997</p>
<p> Issue date			 January 8, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		    February 5, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		    5.2 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids		85.24 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		    5.2 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	     85.24 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity    17.32 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
